      "Equivalent public API list price, used only to estimate cost. Edit freely, then run `tracker reprice` - raw token counts in `events` are never modified.",
      "Model names are matched exactly first, then by longest prefix (e.g. 'claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929' -> 'claude-sonnet-4-5'). Provider prefixes such as 'anthropic/' or 'us.anthropic.' are stripped before matching. If still unmatched, one reasoning-tier suffix (-xhigh, -high, -medium, -low, -tiered-high, -tiered-low) is stripped and matching retried, so one 'gemini-4-neon' entry covers all its variants; an explicit variant entry always wins.",
      "cache_write uses the 5-minute cache-write rate (1.25x input). 1-hour cache writes are billed higher by the API; the tracker does not distinguish them yet.",
      "thinking defaults to the output rate; Claude Code reports thinking inside output_tokens, so its thinking column is usually 0.",
      "Models with no matching entry get cost_usd = NULL and are listed as 'unpriced' in `tracker stats`.",
      "Gemini 4 entries: thinking uses the output rate; cache_write is 0 (no cache-write charge recorded).",
      "gemini-4-argon: the listed 2.0 / 10.0 is the current rate; the standard price from 2026-12-01 is 4.0 input / 20.0 output. The tracker applies one rate to all history, so update this entry (and run `tracker reprice`) when you want the new rate used.",
      "Estimates, not list prices: 'unknown' (events whose log names no model) and 'codex-auto-review' (Codex automatic reviews) use 2.0 input / 10.0 output and thinking / 0.20 cache read / 0 cache write."
    ]
